1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,975
Every gaming group has one.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,002
The Backlog.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:09,708
Video games, tabletop campaigns, board games… all waiting for someday.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,834
Meet NextQuest: your party's shared quest board.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,094
Drop in any game, and it sizes up the effort. Hours, difficulty, even acclaim.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,732
Then everyone gets ten secret votes to spend.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,470
No peer pressure. No hurt feelings.

8
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:29,233
The picker weighs interest, time, and who's around tonight, and names what's next.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,498
Paint the times that work, RSVP, and the session's on the calendar.

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,223
And the burn rate chart shows that mountain… finally shrinking.

11
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,554
NextQuest.

12
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,671
Stop scrolling the backlog. Start playing it.
